WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.450
What breaks in production?

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.978
Zones in workload subscriptions
split the records,

3
00:00:04.978 --> 00:00:08.588
so resolution fails or goes
public; the kit flags them.

4
00:00:08.588 --> 00:00:13.450
An endpoint with no zone group has a record
somebody made by hand, or none at all.

5
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.310
The public path left open means
the private endpoint works,

6
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.225
and so does the internet;
three rules catch it.

7
00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:23.384
Purge protection can't be
turned off once it's on,

8
00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:26.787
which is the point, so the
kit only ever asks for it on.

9
00:00:26.787 --> 00:00:31.676
And configuration isn't resolution: the
records can exist while clients still

10
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:36.550
resolve the public name, which is why Lab
2 runs nslookup from a linked machine.
